      "content": "Traditional virtues like individual responsibility often prioritize self-interest over the collective good, which is dangerous when a society is divided by deep cultural and political fault lines. In a digital age, unchecked autonomy allows misinformation to spread unchecked, eroding the shared reality needed for a functioning democracy. Radical empathy and civic courage are superior because they actively bind us together against the isolating forces of algorithms and tribalism, ensuring that our diverse voices are heard rather than drowned out by the loudest noise.",
